The files in this directory are the pre-made EFI authenticated-variable
updates that bootc copies to <ESP>/loader/keys/auto/ during installation.
systemd-boot then offers a one-time enrollment entry.

systemd-boot looks for these exact names (only *.auth files are copied to the
ESP):

    PK.auth    — Platform Key     (signed by pk_key, containing pk_cert)
    KEK.auth   — Key Exchange Key (signed by pk_key, containing kek_cert)
    db.auth    — Signature Database (signed by kek_key, containing db_cert)

Regenerate these files with efitools (cert-to-efi-sig-list + sign-efi-sig-list)
whenever the key material changes. The db.auth certificate must match the
db_cert supplied to the build; if they diverge the signed image is unbootable.

Any non-*.auth file here (such as this README) is ignored by bootc and is never
copied to the ESP. Do NOT add plain files directly under secureboot-keys/:
bootc requires every entry there to be a directory (each one is a key set), and
fails `bootc install` with "is not a directory" otherwise.
